// only run on tag:v0.3.0 or higher

// create new array
// `#n` creates a new variable, the first arg is the name and the second is the type
// there are: 0 for numbers (?= int), 2 for doubles (?= not supported yet), 3 for strings
#n "name" $0

// see that "" always mean `strings`, and `$` always mean integer values (i32 to be presice)

// assign the number `5` to the var
#= "name" $5

// print it to the console
#o "name"
